  "scope": [
    "The public runner owns each original attempt before fixtures and live trace writes, and shares the worker coordinator with screenshots. Stock page/context/browser fixtures, custom worker options and already-published module contexts receive automatic browser-context traces.",
    "All eight pinned retention spellings are accepted, with native screenshots/snapshots/source/attachment defaults. Live traces, video, invalid modes and unknown options reject explicitly. Raw policy validation precedes context enrollment; the original finalizer still owns a rejected attempt journal.",
    "Context creation published during an active attempt without an original attempt claim produces bounded trace-error and no partial successful ZIP. The original test outcome is preserved; a later explicit attempt may enroll the published context.",
    "Artifact-only readiness, screenshots and worker disposal have separate timeout:0 fixture slots. Slow optional artifact work cannot borrow the original project test/worker fixture budget. Original admitted creation and cleanup remain owned under the external job watchdog.",
    "Existing exact recording/chunk custody and limits remain 128 captures per attempt, 256 outstanding worker captures and 128 live or retiring recordings, supplementing native/host byte limits without an RSS claim."
  ],
  "verification": [
    "All three runtimes pass type/provenance, lifecycle, exact archive, finalizer, coordinator, screenshots, public automatic retention and packed consumers. Actual retries, expected failures, skips, timeout and SIGINT preserve original outcomes and errors.",
    "Each retained public archive passes CRC and the pinned TraceLoader. Browser actions preserve original step IDs/titles; public user-step parentage and exact attached body bytes are asserted. Native snapshots and source policy are verified.",
    "Three actual pinned viewer cases each on headless shell and full Chrome open public traces with actions-only, native-capture and string-default policies. The correct embedded caller line is highlighted with workstation source fallback blocked. The shell viewer uses freshly installed packed-consumer traces.",
    "Seven public boundary cases per runtime verify invalid policy rejection before fixtures/hooks/body, video rejection, original failure through 700 ms artifact disposal and a passing test through 700 ms readiness under a 300 ms project timeout. Negative controls retain the original contaminated outcomes.",
    "Trace-off reporter differential, manual trace differential and 30-case screenshot differential pass across all three runtimes. Source/build/browser/driver hashes stay unchanged throughout the final matrix."
  ],
  "developmentFindings": [
    {
      "reportSha256": "1d47e3bbf2167a362bb6a8a3e6ebead3dd3fac521d632336046850e0281b52f1",
      "condition": "Removing only the worker artifact timeout override adds a teardown error to the original test failure. Restoring the override preserves the original error and successful trace."
    },
    {
      "reportSha256": "63b53cff2326d62cc933c23d1bc28357262d124761270fb278de102a30a979f9",
      "condition": "Injected 700 ms artifact readiness under a 300 ms project timeout prevents a passing test body and marks it timedOut. Separate artifact readiness fixture slots repair that outcome."
    },
    {
      "reportSha256": "201159db374a8b6662134123b5abb5eed0badeb48a968de701db5300336118a9",
      "condition": "The first module fixture probe exposed a silently incomplete runner-only trace when an earlier unclaimed context creation published during an attempt. The coordinator now emits trace-error instead of a successful partial ZIP."
    },
    {
      "reportSha256": "88577c91c3275fa58c57b3b9bca77cfd24291bca0fcaccb2e97dde9317b50f24",
      "condition": "The first repaired-public fixture verifier incorrectly expected the error class in the diagnostic body. The finalizer intentionally publishes the safe data message; the unit check independently verifies the UnsupportedFeatureError class."
    },
    {
      "reportSha256": "b2af47c5b909408faccd168389959f4b8a4d1bb10cf4d0aeeedbf4599238064f",
      "condition": "The first teardown verifier expected stdout text but Bun delivered a base64 buffer. The verifier now normalizes either reporter representation."
    },
    {
      "reportSha256": "935fef56c3041a5bdc92ff02e8c0fa39c329aaeb79cb0c53f6d807b341ddd73d",
      "condition": "The first public viewer adapter assumed all projects share one report suite. It now collects the three project-specific suites."
    },
    {
      "reportSha256": "ee06cfb48eca44fd0567fc1645693c432b5818f99096ccb7156c135aebb0cd08",
      "condition": "The generic manual source viewer check did not expand a public user-step parent. The shared viewer check now accepts an explicit parent title and expands it through normal tree keyboard interaction."
    },
    {
      "reportSha256": "5981c2060e9423ac8575d31c0a7718349bc350a357db200461cf8c5daae617e0",
      "condition": "The preceding 75-group matrix passed before the slow-readiness regression case and actual public viewer adapter were added. The final frozen matrix supersedes that source/build state."
    }
  ],
  "reproduce": [
    "Build all four packages with pinned Bun, run tools/typecheck.mjs and applicable tools/record-*-provenance.mjs --check.",
    "Run tools/test-owned-runner-runtime.mjs, test-trace-recording-lifecycle.mjs, test-runner-trace-archives.mjs, test-runner-trace-finalizer.mjs, test-runner-artifact-coordinator.mjs, test-runner-screenshots.mjs and test-runner-artifact-lifecycle.mjs on Bun and Node22/24.",
    "With explicit accepted FLASHWRIGHT_BROWSER_PATH and FLASHWRIGHT_DRIVER_PATH, run tools/run-runner-artifact-coordinator-tests.mjs OUTPUT --public, then separate OUTPUT directories with --policies, --fixtures, --interruption and --packed --fixtures. Repeat public scenarios on Bun full Chrome and packed policies on Bun.",
    "Run tools/run-runner-public-boundary-tests.mjs OUTPUT, tools/run-runner-trace-off-tests.mjs OUTPUT, tools/run-manual-trace-runner-tests.mjs and tools/run-runner-screenshot-tests.mjs per runtime under external watchdogs.",
    "Run tools/test-runner-public-trace-viewer.mjs PUBLIC_FIXTURE_OUTPUT VIEWER_OUTPUT against packed shell and full-Chrome fixture reports."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "This is experimental supported-browser-context coverage. Live traces, video, unclaimed late module creation and broader unsupported DOM/out-of-process snapshot states are not silently claimed.",
    "Public request.newContext remains explicitly unsupported. Standalone API request tracing must be integrated before that separate public gate; private API implementation is not accepted by this checkpoint.",
    "Browser cases reuse the accepted pre-API trace driver. No fresh combined native API/runner, Rust, full-core, Linux, release package-manager or artifact performance acceptance follows.",
    "No release, publication or fastest-framework claim. The overall practical drop-in and performance goal remains active."
  ]
}
